            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0583" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/905a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sterling</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-19T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>36. The Department i$ informed through the Peruvian Embassy here that Dr. Porras
                    has again postponed sailing and will leave April 26. The Department feels that
                    the delay caused in this manner would be very unfortunate, and the impression
                    created would be most undesirable, in view of the fact that the Chilean
                    delegation is already here. Inquire discreetly, therefore, as to whether it will
                    be <pb facs="0584" n="464" xml:id="pg464"/> possible for the Peruvian Government
                    to instruct Dr. Porras to obtain an earlier sailing, or at least that hi$
                    departure be not again postponed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
